The game has ranges when different stuff happens.  There's a
reason folks discuss early game, mid game, late game, end
game separately.  Even though different folks divide the ranges
differently it does make sense given the differences in game
play over time.

Early game to me is until I have returned from mines end and
the sokoban prize.  Even with a spell caster there's often the
problem that early armor interferes with casting so much of
this phase is learning missile combat, evasion, finding better
AC armor though maybe not armor that interferes with casting.
This is not a time for a Valk to bother with spells.

Mid game to me is until I finish the Castle.  It includes Ft
Ludios if it exists, Medusa, big room if it exists, the Quest.
A spell caster will keep switching to pieces of armor that don't
interfere with spell casting.  If I don't get a good dragon scale
mail from dragons (good equaling either SDSM or GDSM) it
is the second wand wish.  Mid game is for filling out the skill
sets (I don't avoid leveling) and filling out the mundane items of
the ascension kit.  Because of the Quest the mid game gets
the first unique item.  Having cone of cold makes a huge
difference on the Medusa level so it is time for a Valk for use
spells.

Late game to me is Valley of the dead down to finding the
vibrating square.  For symetry it makes sense to call it late
game until the first killing of Rodney.  That way the late game
get the second unique item and the end game starts with the
final unique item.  For me late game is for final exporation and
fine tuning of my ascension kit.  A Valk who uses spells will
have enhanced Attack school and cast as additional combat.

End game to me starts with Rodney or maybe descending
into the scanctum to get the Amulet or maybe leaving the
scanctum with the Amulet.  For me the end game is about
fleeing the dungeon, processing the two easy levels, finding
the bleeping portal on water, learning yet another thing to
prepare for for the next time I make it to Astal.  ;^)  Holding
the Amulet makes spell casting something to use for
backup only, but in this phase much combat is clearing a
path to the Amulet or altar so cost in energy isn't all that
relevant any more.


